{
  "item": "T10",
  "question": "The ten named misses (Z7, Z8, Z17, W10, R1 to R5, R8) and the fold undo bugs: one fresh round, on inputs not read, the rules written before any read and before any build.",
  "rules": {
    "link": "A link is [text](url), [text][label], [text][] or [text] with a non-blank text. Code spans close only on a run of the same number of ticks and hold no links. A line starting [label]: is a definition and holds none. A backslash or ! before the [ makes it no link. The first link touched decides: with a url, inline or from a definition (labels ignore case), Link shows it; with none, Link is lit and opens the Add Link form.",
    "form": "With no url the form wraps the selection as on plain text. With a url, Edit writes [text](new), and Remove Link leaves the text; a definition line is left alone.",
    "lazy": "An empty item, or a number other than 1, under a quote's paragraph line is that paragraph's text: Enter takes the spaces before the caret and starts the quote's next line.",
    "setext": "A setext underline with text above it is a heading, not a paragraph.",
    "newline": "A selection starting at a line's end leaves out the spaces and line breaks up to its next text, for Bold, Italic and for what dims.",
    "undo": "Meta+Z takes back typing done before a field's first fold, and keeps the fold. Meta+Z after a toolbar press over a fold keeps the fold."
  },
